[Music]  anyone who's played a mario party game  in the past 20 years has a good idea of  what to expect from switches Super Mario  Party the Nintendo's latest offers a few  new modes that each at their own  creative spin on the tried and true  formula the fierce competitive nature of  the series earliest titles is back as  Super Mario Party ditches Mario Party 9  and tens cooperative car mechanic and  once again pits players against each  other in a race for stars  the overall goal in Super Mario Party is  to earn 5 gems would you get after  completing each of the games five major  offline modes Mario Party mode features  the series classic formula of bite-sized  games interspersed between rounds of  four-game hijinks the biggest change is  the introduction of character dice  blocks while previous mario party games  utilized virtual 10-sided dice now every  character has two dice blocks one  six-sided and the other unique to them  you have to decide which one to use each  turn for the first time in a Mario Party  game your choice of character is more  than just aesthetic and figuring out the  best time to use a specific dice block  adds a level of strategy to what's  typically been an act of randomness each  of the games for boards requires slight  tweaks to your strategy for reaching the  star but they're all small and don't  feel distinct and since there are only  four in total  Mario party mode grows stale fairly  quickly there are 80 minigames in Super  Mario Party and nearly half rely on the  motion control or Rumble features and  the switches joy cons don't worry  both the motion and Rumble features work  surprisingly well it makes for some of  the most cleverly designed games in the  Mario Party series in nutcases for  example you determine a box's contents  by picking it up and measuring the  severity of your joy Kahn's vibration  the drawback to this is that since Super  Mario Party only supports motion and  Rumble control with a single joy con you  won't be able to play the game in  handheld mode or with a pro controller  partner party mode a super mario party's  reimagining of mario party sixes team  battle mode although similar to mario  party mode and partner party there are  more paths around the board and you need  to actually land onto that spot to get a  star instead of just collecting it while  passing by the minor obstacles from  mario party mode becomes trickier to get  past and partner party because you need  to remain mindful of both you and your  partner this type of consideration and  amount of forethought simply doesn't  exist in mario party mode  two of the other major modes River  survival and soundstage are completely  new to the mario party franchise the  former has you working together with  three others to survive a trip down a  dangerous river while playing co-op  minigames while the latter is an  energetic dance competition where you  slowly play rhythm minigames both co-op  and rhythm minigames lack the heated  competition of other head-to-head  minigames but they do pump up a room  [Music]  super mario party's final major mode  challenge road is the closest the game  has to a single-player campaign you play  through every single minigame with  specific handicaps placed on you to make  each one harder this mode comes very  close to giving Super Mario Party just  the amount of challenge that the game  would need to increase its longevity but  unfortunately you can just skip certain  minigames with no consequence and still  beat the entire road  Super Mario Party also has several  smaller modes and features that aren't  tied to earning the Super Start title  and Mario thon you compete in five  minigames online or off where outlasting  your opponents and time based games earn  two extra points on the tournament  ladder square-off  is also a mini game based tournament but  after each win you're allowed to claim a  territory space the winner is whoever  owns the most spaces at the end of the  match both modes give you a goal to  strive for while playing minigames which  creates extra levels of competition  amongst a group of friends there's also  toads rec room where you can play unique  games that changed based on how you  position your switch and a stickers room  where you can cover a wall in the mural  of stickers you can earn or a lock  through scanning and amiibo although the  option of changing perspectives and  toads rec room is an interesting gimmick  none of the games are really made better  by adjusting how you look at them the  stickers room is not worth it getting  invested as it's just a means to sell  more amoebas it's in Super Mario parties  varied assortment of 80 minigames or  you'll find most of your fun especially  if you've got a full group of three  people to play against it's unfortunate  that mario party mode begins to feel  stale after a while but the new partner  party River survival and soundstage  modes are enjoyable alternatives and  even if the unique character dice blocks  don't drastically changed the game they  do implement small moments of strategy  into a series that has for too long  solely relied on randomness to determine  a winner  [Music]

